1
00:00:01,740 --> 00:00:02,340
Reading

2
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:06,080
The Band That Wasn't

3
00:00:07,440 --> 00:00:11,720
Have you ever wanted to be part of a band as a famous singer or musician?

4
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:16,300
Have you ever dreamed of playing in front of thousands of people at a concert,

5
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:19,500
at which everyone is clapping and appreciating your music?

6
00:00:26,820 --> 00:00:30,960
To be honest, a lot of people attach great importance to becoming rich

7
00:00:30,960 --> 00:00:31,560
and famous.

8
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:34,500
But just how do people form a band?

9
00:00:35,820 --> 00:00:39,560
Many musicians meet and form a band because they like to write

10
00:00:39,560 --> 00:00:40,940
and play their own music.

11
00:00:49,740 --> 00:00:53,200
Sometimes they may play to passers-by in the street or subway

12
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:56,980
so that they can earn some extra money for themselves or to pay

13
00:00:56,980 --> 00:00:57,980
for their instruments.

14
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:02,360
Later they may give performances in pubs or clubs,

15
00:01:02,360 --> 00:01:04,220
for which they are paid in cash.

16
00:01:05,160 --> 00:01:11,200
Of course they hope to make records in a studio and sell millions of copies to become millionaires!

17
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:15,620
However, there was one band that started in a different way.

18
00:01:20,780 --> 00:01:24,900
The musicians were to play jokes on each other as well as play music,

19
00:01:25,360 --> 00:01:28,040
most of which was based loosely on the Beatles.

20
00:01:28,960 --> 00:01:34,340
The TV organizers had planned to find four musicians who could act as well as sing.

21
00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:38,940
They put an advertisement in a newspaper looking for rock musicians,

22
00:01:38,960 --> 00:01:42,060
but they could only find one who was good enough.

23
00:01:42,780 --> 00:01:46,380
They had to use actors for the other three members of the band.

24
00:01:47,300 --> 00:01:50,280
As some of these actors could not sing well enough,

25
00:01:50,540 --> 00:01:53,780
they had to rely on other musicians to help them.

26
00:01:54,520 --> 00:01:58,320
So during the broadcasts they just pretended to sing.

27
00:01:59,100 --> 00:02:03,380
Anyhow their performances were humorous enough to be copied by other groups.

28
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:09,080
They were so popular that their fans formed clubs in order to get more familiar

29
00:02:09,080 --> 00:02:09,920
with them.

30
00:02:27,890 --> 00:02:32,540
Then they produced their own records and started touring and playing their own music.

31
00:02:33,260 --> 00:02:39,220
In the USA they became even more popular than the Beatles and sold even more records.

32
00:02:46,820 --> 00:02:49,720
They produced a new record in 1996,

33
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:53,680
with which they celebrated their former time as a real band.
